<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT RISES 1.21 PCT IN WEEK.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT RISES 1.21 PCT IN WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian banks' internal credit</p>
<p>rose to 1,139.2 billion levs on August 30 from 1,125.6 billion</p>
<p>levs a week earlier, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Credit to the government inched up 0.25 percent to 473.5</p>
<p>billion levs, credit to state firms rose 0.80 percent to 303</p>
<p>billion levs and lev-denominated credit to private firms fell</p>
<p>1.06 percent to 130.7 billion levs.</p>
<p> PERCENTAGE CHANGE	 AUG 30-AUG 23   AUG 30-JULY 26</p>
<p> Total internal credit	 +1.21	     +4.70</p>
<p> Credit to govt		  +0.25	     +2.98</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	 +0.80	     +5.91</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms -1.06	     +2.43</p>
<p> NOMINAL (BILLION LEVS)	AUG 30    AUG 23   JULY 26</p>
<p> Total internal credit	1,139.2   1,125.6   1,088.1 </p>
<p> Credit to govt		   473.5     472.3     459.8</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	  303.0     300.6     286.1</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms  130.7     132.1     125.1</p>
<p>Dlr credit to private firms</p>
<p> (USD billion)		    $1.15	$1.13    $1.16</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
